## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: In QA-2 the local user joins after the others have started and waves; the colleagues acknowledge it, and the leader says "Hi. We just got started."
  date: 2026-10-18
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-2: In QA-2 the leader shares the DXOS Architecture "Plugin metrics" sheet, which is maximised with the call view's expand control, and edits its chart to switch off horizontal bars.
  date: 2026-10-19
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-3: A simulated call's scripted lines are written to the active meeting's transcript as live transcription would write them. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  why: Without live transcription in a simulated call, the transcript would stay empty and QA-2 could not check it.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-4: QA-2 makes the meeting active before adding the colleagues, and binds the seam's transcript to the script's lines under display names, with the leader's screenshare. Fills in [D-2] and [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  why: An agent runs QA-2's invoke literally, so it must match the operation's input and the active meeting.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A call's transcript comes from RealtimeKit's native transcription: CallManager emits only the local speaker's final segments, and this plugin owns the transcription flag (its own call activity), the feed and enrichment, writing through one queued TranscriptSink that resolves the active meeting's feed per segment. The meeting payload carries only the meeting id, and QA-3 checks the sink offline.
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.2, F-3, HandlePayload, SetTranscription, MeetingState, T-4, T-7, QA-3]
  why: plugin-calls is meeting-agnostic, per-segment appends could land out of order, and a feed DXN beside the meeting id duplicated what `meeting.transcript.feed` already names.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14186
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A Meeting's own call offers the Start/Stop transcription toggle in MeetingArticle's toolbar, and both toggles (channel call and meeting) share op:SetTranscription. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-3.6, MeetingArticle, SetTranscription]
  why: The toggle existed only on channel calls, so a call started from a Meeting's Call tab could not turn transcription on.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14186
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The meeting payload names the meeting by its absolute URI, which HandlePayload parses as an EID, and CallExtension activates only once the client is initialized, since it subscribes to the call manager. QA-4 checks the live path. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [HandlePayload, SetActive, QA-4]
  why: HandlePayload read the URI as a `space:object` id, so every call-state update cleared the active meeting and the sink dropped each segment; and CallExtension could start before the manager existed, which disabled the whole plugin.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14186
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The live meeting stories share one story file that loads the meeting plugin with all its dependencies and one hardcoded meeting id, so every live story connects to the same meeting; it includes a plain call story.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [QA-4]
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The hardcoded meeting is the call room `storybook:plugin-meeting:standup` on the preview EDGE, which names both the call's swarm and its RealtimeKit meeting, so every tab running the stories joins one call; each tab keeps its own identity, bound to a test account, and its own meeting hub, and the story's toolbar makes that hub the call's active meeting when it starts transcription. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [QA-4]
  why: Stories boot a fresh identity and space per tab, so only the call can be shared without an invitation; MeetingArticle offers its transcription toggle only in the meeting's own room, which a fixed room is not.
  rejected:
    - Share one meeting object across tabs: needs a space invitation between story tabs.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: The Meeting story shows the meeting as Composer does, one article; a fresh load makes a new space, and an invitation lets another tab join that space so both render the same meeting. The Call and CallTranscription stories stay as they are, with a shared call and transcript but separate spaces.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [QA-5]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The Meeting story's meeting lives in its own open space, since an identity's default space is created locked to its owner; the invite is a standing multi-use invitation with no auth step, carried to the guest as the story's `invitation` arg, and the guest joins instead of seeding a meeting. Every story uses Composer's EDGE features (signaling and the subduction and feed replicators), so a guest receives the space's objects and the transcript feed. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [QA-5]
  why: The default space refuses invitations, and without the replicators an invited tab sees the space but none of its objects.
  rejected:
    - Invite through the space plugin's members dialog: loads the space plugin and its navigation only to share.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The MeetingTranscript story is deleted.
  date: 2026-11-11
